    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the soft-delete of owners:\n\n## Changes\n\n**Domain model**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a primitive `boolean deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)` accessors and a `toString()` entry. A new owner defaults to `false`.\n\n**Persistence schema** (all four dialects, so the entity mapping is consistent everywhere)\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table. (HSQLDB \u2014 the profile the tests run under \u2014 requires `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`.) Existing `data.sql` seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they pick up the default.\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` property to the `Owner` schema (and to its `required` list), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and `MapStruct` maps it by name. It surfaces on both GET and POST responses.\n\n**Deletion behavior**\n- `rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 now flags the owner deleted and `save()`s it instead of removing the row. The existing DELETE pipeline (transaction-governed, `RespondWithNoContent`) still returns 204, and GET afterward returns the retained owner with `deleted: true`.\n\n**Ignoring deleted owners in create-time checks**\n- `repository/OwnerRepository.java` \u2014 added a single-source-of-truth `default findAllActive()` that filters out soft-deleted owners.\n- Switched the **duplicate check** (`EnsureUniqueHousehold`, `PossibleDuplicates`) and the **identity checks** (`CountNamesakes`, `CountHouseholdMembers`, `AssignCustomerCode`) from `findAll()` to `findAllActive()`. The capacity/rate checks (`EnsureCityCapacity`, `DailyRegistrations`) and the list endpoint (`ListOwners`) intentionally stay on `findAll()` \u2014 they're neither duplicate nor identity checks.\n\nThe audit log during the run confirms the behavior end-to-end: the owner re-created after a soft-delete reuses the deleted owner's deterministic customer code (`NSW-16E6609E`) with no `-2` suffix, proving the deleted record no longer influences identity assignment.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 full suite green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).",
